          "lines": [
            578,
            645
          ]
        }
      ],
      "independent_controls": [
        "RA-T04"
      ],
      "limits": "Exact arithmetic representability control only. Compiled dependency overflow behavior was not run; the report does not choose panic or wrap as the observed result.",
      "next_action": "Use arbitrary-precision accumulation or checked arithmetic with an explicit refusal, and retain unavailable metrics as unavailable."
    },
    {
      "id": "RAD-F05",
      "title": "Scheduler status and completion are not enforced task outcomes.",
      "assessment": "SceneSpec validates allowed_result_statuses, but scheduler.advance checks scene identity without checking membership in that set or assigned producer identity. A terminal scene becomes COMPLETED for any non-stop status: with allowed PASS and empty stop list, an incoming HOLD becomes COMPLETED. Continuation halt similarly marks any nonempty history COMPLETED. complete_bout uses a fixed PASS/changed_state=1 completion input for traversal.",
      "priority": "P1",
      "source_evidence": [
