      "assessment": "Full authorization algorithm read plus exact generated-trailer transfer. The gate binds selected candidate/check content refs, requires a NON_BLOCKING critique label, distinguishes declared/unmeasured/open carriers, protects contexts, keeps ablated/fixture outcomes non-authorized, and authorizes only the AUTHORIZED branch. It explicitly delegates authenticity/reproduction of checker facts to the preceding use case. It chooses the first unblocked candidate, not the first fully checked one; critique-verdict strings and measurement context remain supplied premises. Ablation flags use Python truthiness, including nonempty false-like strings. Candidate selection remains authority None. Several emitted DDC carrier hashes are the constant hash of carrier rather than the actual carrier; event_kind may say TERMINAL while terminal flag is false, which requires downstream interpretation. Generated count-template does not strengthen these operational claims; no gate/emitter was executed.",
