      "review_level": "full_owner_prefix_plus_exact_pinned_template_and_complete_residual_review",
      "assessment": "Complete1077-line prefix plus exact template. Actual finite mechanisms: alphabet/prefix syntax, sequence/parent continuity, step/rollback bookkeeping and bounded-i64 rational metric admission. Important limits: step record hash omits phi/gamma/timestamp, compensation record binds only branch ID/count rather than step bodies, and class hashes hash labels rather than actual states. Adjacent before/after class equality is not enforced. Missing metrics become zero histories; window sums use unchecked Rational64 addition, so individually representable metrics do not ensure a representable sum. OEARS M is terminal in transition rule but complete validation globally requires final T, making a completed M refusal impossible. Compensation steps are not DFA-checked; rollback accepts any in-range index, not only saved checkpoints. JSONL record hashes and expected head are optional, blank lines affect physical sequence indices, and evaluator deserialization has no custom invariant revalidation. No cryptographic collision is asserted: omitted fields simply do not enter hash material. No native execution.",
